{"id": 63, "ts": 1780435866.4008102, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 4, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I appreciate Sarah\u2019s confidence in Candidate\u202fC, especially given his quick decision\u2011making and strong attention skills. However, James just confirmed that C \u201chas difficulty communicating ideas\u201d and is \u201cregarded as egocentric,\u201d and we have no evidence of his crew\u2011cooperation ability. In a long\u2011distance cockpit, clear, collaborative communication is non\u2011negotiable; a pilot who struggles to convey ideas or is perceived as self\u2011centered could jeopardize crew coordination under pressure.\nBy contrast, Candidate\u202fB is described as very conscientious, handles stress very well, and assesses weather conditions expertly\u2014key for reliability and stress resilience on international routes. While B is sometimes noted as \u201cpretentious\u201d and may \u201cadopt the wrong tone,\u201d these issues appear less severe than a fundamental communication barrier, and we have no indication that they impair his overall crew interaction.\nGiven the critical weight of professional communication and crew cooperation, I\u2019m shifting my provisional recommendation to **Candidate\u202fB**. I believe B offers a more balanced profile across the essential safety criteria."}
